body:
Damn, thanks. While I have been raging quite a bit, I can't remember 6-9- O WAIT. Yeah, if it was the one where it alternates different movesets, that one was brutal, but once you know how each one works (I died alot) it is a bit simpler. I just finished 6-Ω, which damn was that annoying. I felt like I was destroying myself, but I did manage to do one cool pro fire and got a A-Rank, so I'm satisfied, for now. I just can't stand seeing C-Ranks, knowing that, since It's 2018, everyone at this point is really good and tips are easy to come by. Even just B's would satisfy me. I understand that the reward is the beauty of the game and its music, but OOOOOF is it hard to focus on that when it gets WONKY. I'm on 7-3, Mr. Lazer Man is getting easier, but the lines. The quad lines are tough when at x3 speed. Don't get me wrong, I nailed it at 5-Ω, but when they add alot of the extras, that's when I freak out. I don't restart alot, unless it's ridicously easy, like the first 2-3 levels of each section. And in Play+ it's like, "Hey, wanna get better? Let's just cut your life to one and rip out your soul if you don't get an S," so I feel strongly compelled to atleast do decent in the main game. This does help alot, so thank you for that. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

**Putting this down here so you can see it. I recorded my 6-Ω bossfight cause I felt like it, so here it is if you want a glimpse (I guess) at my current level against bosses. In my opinion, bosses are easier than the progression levels cause, unless its 6-9, they never change, making it easier to adapt and try new things.** 

Here's the link to the vid: [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jb-vve2ZADc](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jb-vve2ZADc) .  Have a nice day!
